      "content": "Since you are accustomed to high doses, care is still essential because individual tolerance varies significantly. Generally, a safe upper limit for supplemental caffeine in a single sitting is often cited around 400mg, though this can be higher for some. Regarding green tea extract, doses vary widely by product, but many studies use ranges between 300mg to 500mg combined with caffeine. Always prioritize physician advice over self-optimization when aiming for maximum dosage.",
